{
  "slug": "vibe-test",
  "name": "Vibe Test",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "Test coverage for vibe-coded apps that actually matters. vibe-test reads your app, classifies it by type and deployment risk, and generates tests proportional to that risk — not a boilerplate dump, not a pass/fail meter. It catches the broken harnesses other tools assume away: runners that silently report 0%, missing test binaries, coverage cherry-picked over a fraction of your files. Seven commands cover audit, generate, fix, coverage, gate, and posture, and the handoff artifacts (test plan, runbook, CI stub) survive uninstalling the plugin. JS/TS today.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **14 skills** and **8 commands**.\n\n- **Skills** (14): `audit` (Use when the user says `/vibe-test:audit` or wants the gap analysis — 'audit my tests', 'where are my…), `coverage` (Use when the user says `/vibe-test:coverage` or wants the honest number — 'what's my real coverage', 'measure coverage',…), `decay` (Internal SKILL — not a slash command), `evolve` (This skill should be used when the user says \\\"/vibe-test:evolve\\\" — reflective Level-3 loop for Vibe Test itself), `fix` (Use when the user says `/vibe-test:fix` or reports broken testing — 'my tests are failing', 'the suite is…), `friction-logger` (Internal SKILL — not a slash command), `gate` (Use when the user says `/vibe-test:gate` or wants tier enforcement — 'should CI pass', 'block merges below the…), `generate` (Use when the user says `/vibe-test:generate` or asks for the missing tests to be written — 'write the…), and 6 more\n- **Commands** (8): `audit` (Audit — inventory + classify + score), `coverage` (Coverage — honest-denominator measurement with adaptation-prompt UX), `evolve` (Evolve — reflective Level-3 loop for Vibe Test itself), `fix` (Fix — diagnose broken tests and harnesses, route repairs by confidence), `gate` (Gate — single pass/fail for tier enforcement), `generate` (Generate — turn audit findings into test files), `posture` (Posture — read-only ambient summary), `vibe-test` (Router — identity, state-awareness, next-step prompt)\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install vibe-test@claude-community` from `estevanhernandez-stack-ed/vibe-test` (`packages/vibe-test`).",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude"
  ],
  "pluginType": "package",
  "package": {
    "skill": 14,
    "command": 8
  },
